_terms":["environment","jewish-outreach","partnership","public-service"],"relations":[],"canonical_file":"data/items/living-torah-aid-318996.json","documented_circumstances":null,"question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["Stable Living Torah item-level player record; audiovisual content remains unverified."],"conditions_or_qualifications":[],"audience":null,"verification_scope":"publisher metadata/summary only","witness_provenance":"JEM/Living Torah published video player","evidence_family_id":null,"primary_secondary_status":null,"has_content_evidence":true,"proposition_origin":"editorial_summary_derived","proposition_verbatim":false,"evidence_integrity_issues":[],"search_text":"Partnership for a Jewish Environment Stable Living Torah item-level player record; audiovisual content remains unverified. Video 5 Cheshvan 5752 / October 13, 1991 unknown environment jewish-outreach partnership public-service Stable Living Torah item-level player record; audiovisual content remains unverified."},{"key":"url:https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2243668/jewish/Advice-concerning-the-response-to-a-medical-issue-the-importance-of-bitachon-trust-in-G-d.htm","id":"igrot-kodesh-letter-872","title":"אגרת מס׳ 872 — מענה בעניין מצב רפואי וביטחון בה׳","summary":"The published page identifies this as Letter No. 872, dated 23 Teves 5711, to an unnamed recipient. The letter explicitly says it responds to a letter from Thursday of Parshas Vayechi reporting several operations. The incoming letter itself is not reproduced. Letter No. 937 later contains an editorial cross-reference to Letter No. 872 and its cited sources in connection with the Chabad maxim 'Tracht gut, vet zain gut'.","source_class":"Igrot Kodesh","status":"Linked","canonical_status":"Linked","context_status":"partial","context_status_raw":null,"date":"5711-10-23","language":"English translation of Hebrew/Yiddish correspondence","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2243668/jewish/Advice-concerning-the-response-to-a-medical-issue-the-importance-of-bitachon-trust-in-G-d.htm","aid":null,"locator":null,"rights_status":"copyrighted-source; bounded research paraphrases and link only; no protected full text copied","publisher_terms":["medical issue","bitachon","health"],"research_terms":["health guidance","trust in G-d","response to reported medical treatment","attention management","practical directives"],"relations":[{"type":"editorial_cross_reference","target_id":"igrot-kodesh-letter-937","basis":"Footnote 2 of published Letter No. 937 explicitly directs the reader to Letter No. 872 and the sources cited there in connection with 'Tracht gut, vet zain gut'."}],"canonical_file":"data/items/igrot-kodesh-letter-872.json","documented_circumstances":"Letter No. 872, dated 23 Teves 5711, to an unnamed recipient who reported having undergone several operations; the incoming wording and diagnosis are absent.","question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["The medical guidance combines following physicians' instructions with avoiding self-directed immersion in medical literature that increases fear and despair.","The recipient is advised to redirect attention from repeated health analysis toward trust in G-d and regular, expanded study of Chassidus.","The response links personal strengthening with communal action through classes, gatherings and financing a substantial chassidic publication."],"conditions_or_qualifications":[],"audience":null,"verification_scope":"The authorized publisher's English translation was inspected. Propositions are bounded paraphrases of the outgoing response; the diagnosis, incoming letter, physical original and original-language witness were not inspected. This is historical-source description, not medical advice.","witness_provenance":"Sichos in English English translation published on Chabad.org; underlying original manuscript not inspected","evidence_family_id":"original-letter-aid-2243668","primary_secondary_status":"authorized publisher English translation by Eli Touger; derived, non-independent witness","has_content_evidence":true,"proposition_origin":"source_grounded_paraphrase","proposition_verbatim":false,"evidence_integrity_issues":[],"proposition_verification":"source_text_inspected","proposition_source_locator":"publisher translation, lines 278-285: medical response, attention guidance, trust, study and communal action","search_text":"אגרת מס׳ 872 — מענה בעניין מצב רפואי וביטחון בה׳ The published page identifies this as Letter No. 872, dated 23 Teves 5711, to an unnamed recipient. The letter explicitly says it responds to a letter from Thursday of Parshas Vayechi reporting several operations. The incoming letter itself is not reproduced. Letter No. 937 later contains an editorial cross-reference to Letter No. 872 and its cited sources in connection with the Chabad maxim 'Tracht gut, vet zain gut'. Igrot Kodesh 5711-10-23 English translation of Hebrew/Yiddish correspondence medical issue bitachon health health guidance trust in G-d response to reported medical treatment attention management practical directives The medical guidance combines following physicians' instructions with avoiding self-directed immersion in medical literature that increases fear and despair. The recipient is advised to redirect attention from repeated health analysis toward trust in G-d and regular, expanded study of Chassidus. The response links personal strengthening with communal action through classes, gatherings and financing a substantial chassidic publication."},{"key":"url:https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2244167/jewish/An-allusion-in-the-letters-associated-with-the-Hebrew-year-5711.htm","id":"igrot-kodesh-letter-926","title":"Letter No. 926 — reply concerning a scheduled meeting and an allusion to the year 5711","summary":"The public item page identifies the recipient as R. Efraim Eliezer HaKohen Yolles and states that the letter responds to his report that a meeting had been scheduled concerning his affairs. The incoming letter is not present. The response asks to be informed of good news and develops a Torah allusion associated with the year 5711.","source_class":"Igrot Kodesh","status":"Indexed","canonical_status":"Indexed","context_status":"partial","context_status_raw":null,"date":"5711-22-Adar-I","language":"English translation of original correspondence","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2244167/jewish/An-allusion-in-the-letters-associated-with-the-Hebrew-year-5711.htm","aid":null,"locator":null,"rights_status":"copyrighted-source; bounded research paraphrases and link only; no protected full text copied","publisher_terms":["5711","correspondence"],"research_terms":["response to incoming report","request for follow-up news","Torah allusion"],"relations":[],"canonical_file":"data/items/igrot-kodesh-letter-926.json","documented_circumstances":"Letter No. 926 to R. Efraim Eliezer HaKohen Yolles, dated 22 Adar I 5711, responding to news of a scheduled meeting concerning his affairs.","question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["The writer asks to be informed of favorable results from a scheduled meeting so that he may share the recipient's joy.","The response connects the Torah phrase about raising the heads of Israel with a letter-play allusion to the Hebrew year 5711.","It justifies the allusion through the traditional principle that a word's received reading can support interpretation even when a letter is not written."],"conditions_or_qualifications":[],"audience":null,"verification_scope":"The authorized publisher's English translation and its editorial notes were inspected. Propositions are bounded paraphrases; the incoming letter, meeting record, physical original and original-language witness were not inspected.","witness_provenance":"Chabad.org / Sichos in English published translation; identifies Letter No. 926","evidence_family_id":"original-letter-aid-2244167","primary_secondary_status":"authorized publisher English translation by Eli Touger; derived, non-independent witness","has_content_evidence":true,"proposition_origin":"source_grounded_paraphrase","proposition_verbatim":false,"evidence_integrity_issues":[],"proposition_verification":"source_text_inspected","proposition_source_locator":"publisher translation, lines 272-294: addressee, meeting response and year-5711 allusion with editorial note","search_text":"Letter No. 926 — reply concerning a scheduled meeting and an allusion to the year 5711 The public item page identifies the recipient as R. Efraim Eliezer HaKohen Yolles and states that the letter responds to his report that a meeting had been scheduled concerning his affairs. The incoming letter is not present. The response asks to be informed of good news and develops a Torah allusion associated with the year 5711. Igrot Kodesh 5711-22-Adar-I English translation of original correspondence 5711 correspondence response to incoming report request for follow-up news Torah allusion The writer asks to be informed of favorable results from a scheduled meeting so that he may share the recipient's joy. The response connects the Torah phrase about raising the heads of Israel with a letter-play allusion to the Hebrew year 5711. It justifies the allusion through the traditional principle that a word's received reading can support interpretation even when a letter is not written."},{"key":"url:https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2271629/jewish/Assurance-that-the-Rebbe-Rayatz-will-respond-to-the-panim-brought-to-him-to-Think-positively-and-the-outcome-will-be-good.htm","id":"igrot-kodesh-letter-937","title":"Letter No. 937 — response to two letters and two panim; positive thought and speech regarding illness","summary":"Published correspondence page identifies the recipient as R. Yisrael Noach Bilenitzky and states that the letter responds to two undated letters and two enclosed panim. The response includes assurance that the panim will be read at the Rebbe Rayatz's gravesite and guidance against severe/exaggerated speech about illness, explicitly invoking 'Tracht gut, vet zain gut'. The incoming letters and panim are not present on the public page, so the initiating situation remains only partially recoverable.","source_class":"Igrot Kodesh","status":"Linked","canonical_status":"Linked","context_status":"partial","context_status_raw":null,"date":"5711-Adar-II-Rosh-Chodesh-day-1","language":"English translation of original correspondence","source_url":"https://www.chabad.org/therebbe/letters/default_cdo/aid/2271629/jewish/Assurance-that-the-Rebbe-Rayatz-will-respond-to-the-panim-brought-to-him-to-Think-positively-and-the-outcome-will-be-good.htm","aid":null,"locator":null,"rights_status":"copyrighted-source; bounded research paraphrases and link only; no protected full text copied","publisher_terms":["health","bitachon","pan","Rebbe Rayatz"],"research_terms":["response to incoming correspondence","illness framing","positive thought","speech and writing","prayer request"],"relations":[{"type":"editorial_cross_reference","target_id":"igrot-kodesh-letter-872","basis":"The published footnote to the phrase 'Tracht gut, vet zain gut' explicitly directs the reader to Letter No. 872 and its sources. Letter 872 is now item-level indexed in the canonical repository."}],"canonical_file":"data/items/igrot-kodesh-letter-937.json","documented_circumstances":"Letter No. 937 to R. Yisrael Noach Bilenitzky, dated first day of Rosh Chodesh Adar II 5711, responding to two undated letters and two enclosed petitions.","question_or_problem":null,"response_propositions":["The response promises to read petitions for the recipient's wife and grandson at the Previous Rebbe's gravesite and expresses hope for their recovery.","It criticizes severe or exaggerated speech and writing about illness, extending the maxim of positive thought to spoken and written expression.","The closing inte